# Keep it simple

## Decision test

If two approaches work, choose the one with:

- Fewer files
- Fewer dependencies
- Fewer runtime modes (dev/mock/prod paths should share code)
- No new env vars unless necessary

## Patterns already chosen for simplicity

- `fetch` instead of SDK (ADR-0002)
- Filename registry instead of manual maps (ADR-0004)
- `seed.ts` single source instead of duplicated mocks (ADR-0012)
- `global.css` tokens instead of Tailwind JS config (ADR-0008)

## Red flags

- Adding a dependency to save ten lines
- Introducing a "core" or "shared" package inside the repo
- Abstract factories for sections with only three variants
- Configuration JSON driving what TypeScript could express

Simple code is easier for the next clone — and for agents editing the template.
